  "notes": "0.1.737b\n\nRuntime heater/cooler diagnostic results now follow their unique runtime test\nrequest ID. Fresh results remain usable after long uptime gaps and millis\nrollover; zero, duplicate, older and cross-load replays are rejected. The\ncooler reference-unavailable result is correlated to the same request.\nRuntime evidence reads and cancellation also verify request origin, so a UART\nrequest with the same numeric ID cannot be mistaken for the runtime pulse.\nUART cancellation cannot cancel an unrelated runtime pulse with a colliding\nID; the universal safety-stop paths retain their behavior.\n\nCurrent limits, diagnostic pulse durations, sensor configuration, learned\nflashlight settings, BLE memory admission and animation cadence are unchanged.\nAn unavailable matching cooler reference remains inconclusive and cannot clear\na confirmed fault. This does not claim recovery of a missing sensor.\n",
